# Trellis workflow state.
#
# There are TWO .gitignore files involved. They have different scopes and
# responsibilities; they are NOT duplicates:
#
#   1. .trellis/.gitignore   (generated by `trellis init`, do not hand-edit)
#      - Scope: only .trellis/ and below.
#      - Responsibility: Trellis' own local/runtime files (.developer,
#        .current-task, .runtime/, *.tmp, .backup-*, __pycache__, ...).
#      - It deliberately does NOT decide the commit policy for spec/, tasks/,
#        workspace/, scripts/ or workflow.md; that choice is left to the project.
#
#   2. This file (project-owned).
#      - Scope: whole repository, paths anchored with `/` at repo root so they
#        cannot accidentally match a same-named path deeper in the tree.
#      - Responsibility: the project's commit policy for the Trellis content
#        that .trellis/.gitignore intentionally leaves open.
#
# Policy: this project COMMITS its Trellis knowledge so that a fresh
# `git clone` restores the full project standard and working progress:
#
#   .trellis/spec/        coding contracts (NOT regenerable by `trellis init`)
#   .trellis/tasks/       task PRDs, designs, research and progress
#   .trellis/workspace/   per-developer journals and session traces
#   .trellis/workflow.md  development workflow definition
#   .trellis/config.yaml  Trellis project config
#   .trellis/agents/      sub-agent (check/implement) definitions
#
# Only regenerable Trellis internals and local/runtime scratch are ignored.
# `trellis init` rebuilds these from the installed CLI package.
#
# Note: .gitignore rules can only ignore; they cannot un-ignore a path whose
# parent directory is already excluded. Keep the entries below path-anchored
# (`/.trellis/...`) so a project subdirectory named e.g. `scripts/` stays tracked.
/.trellis/scripts/
/.trellis/.version
/.trellis/.template-hashes.json
/.trellis/.gitignore

# Local-only Trellis state, already covered inside .trellis/ today but listed
# here too so the intent is explicit and survives a regenerated nested file.
/.trellis/.developer
/.trellis/.current-task
/.trellis/.runtime/
/.trellis/.agents/
/.trellis/.agent-log
/.trellis/.session-id
/.trellis/.plan-log
/.trellis/.ralph-state.json

# One-shot bootstrap scaffolding; no project value after initial setup.
/.trellis/tasks/00-bootstrap-guidelines/

# Trellis task scratch space: file staging / patch snapshots / session trace dumps.
# Only the task's own deliverables (task.json, prd.md, design.md, implement.md,
# research/, check.jsonl) are meant to be committed.
/.trellis/tasks/**/staging/
/.trellis/tasks/**/*.patch
/.trellis/tasks/**/*.diff
/.trellis/tasks/**/.backup-*/
/.trellis/tasks/**/*.jsonl.tmp
/.trellis/tasks/**/__pycache__/

# Local diagnostic exports and shell inspection fragments
/_*.txt
/tmp_*.txt
/s[1-5].txt
/rc[1-2].txt
/run_chunk.txt
/corelist.txt
/lib_tree.txt
/.dsh_*.txt
/.dsh_tmp/
/.gitstatus.txt
/.gs.txt
/.st.txt
